body:
The 2M-case fuzz with all classes linked aborts under ASan+UBSan on the first V18 word:

  gpu/hwcodec/emu/n2a32_neon_3same.c:329:13: runtime error: shift exponent 64 is too large for 64-bit type uint64_t

Context (saturating shift path, esize==64):
  if (esize == 64) {
      if ((b >> (64 - (unsigned)sh)) != 0) { set_qc(c); return mask; }
      return b << (unsigned)sh;
  }
When sh == 0 this is b >> 64. A saturating shift by 0 must return b unchanged. Please handle sh==0 before the test (and check the sibling `v << s` / other 64-bit shift sites for the same issue; the first abort is this line). I cannot give the exact random A32 word because the sanitizer aborts before the trial print; it is reproducible with the fuzz command below in <1 s, so any seed will hit it. Build/run:
  clang -std=c11 -O1 -g -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=all -pthread -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE -I gpu/hwcodec/include -I gpu/hwcodec/tests/emu gpu/hwcodec/emu/n2a32_*.c gpu/hwcodec/tests/emu/fuzz.c -lm -o /tmp/fuzz && /tmp/fuzz --a32 1000000 --t32 1000000
No other sanitizer report appears before this one. This blocks run_fuzz acceptance until fixed.
